-- The Armv8-M corpus lane's machine: QEMU's mps2-an505, whose Cortex-M33
-- executes the corpus built at armv8-m.main (D607).  This describes an
-- emulator's map for the lane, not a chip, and only the lane's entry-module
-- file, lanes/lane-mps2-an505.ldn, imports it (D619).  It names the core,
-- the table's length and, beside this file, the memory; no interrupt is
-- named, since no corpus program takes one.

compiler.device("mps2-an505")
compiler.core("cortex-m33")
compiler.vectors(48)
